1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,908
A shortcode is a small tag in square brackets that you type into

2
00:00:04,908 --> 00:00:06,304
the text of a page.

3
00:00:06,304 --> 00:00:09,430
The site replaces it with a picture or an address.

4
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:14,510
In this video, you insert an image, set its options, and pick shortcodes from a list.

5
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:22,290
Some of what a page shows depends on the site, such as a

6
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:24,188
picture from the media library.

7
00:00:24,188 --> 00:00:27,727
You type a shortcode in the text, and the site replaces it with

8
00:00:27,727 --> 00:00:29,933
the result when it displays the page.

9
00:00:29,933 --> 00:00:32,190
The editor keeps the shortcode itself.

10
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:36,302
A shortcode starts with a name in square brackets.

11
00:00:36,302 --> 00:00:41,466
Options can follow the name, and some shortcodes take content between an opening

12
00:00:41,466 --> 00:00:43,148
tag and a closing tag.

13
00:00:43,148 --> 00:00:46,450
For an image, that content is the name of a file.

14
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:52,812
With the Shortcodes feature enabled, the Media module adds the image shortcode, which

15
00:00:52,812 --> 00:00:58,116
shows a picture, and the asset_url shortcode, which gives the address of a file.

16
00:00:58,116 --> 00:01:04,530
The locale shortcode shows its content for a matching language, and needs the Localization module.

17
00:01:08,732 --> 00:01:12,252
The Article list shows each article with an Edit button.

18
00:01:12,252 --> 00:01:13,445
Let's open one.

19
00:01:13,445 --> 00:01:17,589
Its body is a text editor, and the toolbar has buttons named Insert

20
00:01:17,589 --> 00:01:19,462
Shortcode and Insert Media.

21
00:01:19,918 --> 00:01:23,794
Let's add a picture after the line that introduces the photo.

22
00:01:23,794 --> 00:01:28,306
Insert Media opens the media library in a dialog, with its files listed.

23
00:01:28,306 --> 00:01:31,198
Each file you select adds its own shortcode.

24
00:01:31,652 --> 00:01:34,543
We select home-bg.jpg and confirm.

25
00:01:34,543 --> 00:01:39,168
The dialog closes, and the text holds the image shortcode:

26
00:01:39,168 --> 00:01:44,082
the name in square brackets, the file name, and a closing tag.

27
00:01:44,533 --> 00:01:46,101
Publish saves the change.

28
00:01:46,101 --> 00:01:50,197
On the published page, the site has replaced the shortcode with the picture

29
00:01:50,197 --> 00:01:51,663
from the media library.

30
00:01:55,863 --> 00:01:57,838
Options go after the name.

31
00:01:57,838 --> 00:02:03,267
The image shortcode takes alt, for alternative text, and class, for a style class.

32
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:07,401
Width and height ask for a resized copy in the sizes the site

33
00:02:07,401 --> 00:02:11,103
accepts, and mode, format and quality shape that copy.

34
00:02:12,691 --> 00:02:15,947
Let's ask for a copy that is 480 pixels wide.

35
00:02:15,947 --> 00:02:21,691
Inside the opening tag, after the name, we type the width option with the value 480.

36
00:02:22,148 --> 00:02:23,785
Next comes the alt option.

37
00:02:23,785 --> 00:02:27,521
Its text describes the picture for visitors who can't see it, so we

38
00:02:27,521 --> 00:02:29,108
type a short description.

39
00:02:29,559 --> 00:02:32,932
After publishing, the page shows a smaller picture.

40
00:02:32,932 --> 00:02:36,659
The site served a copy resized to the width we asked for.

41
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:43,753
Insert Shortcode opens Available Shortcodes.

42
00:02:43,753 --> 00:02:48,022
Each shortcode is a card, with a hint and a note on how to write it.

43
00:02:48,022 --> 00:02:50,849
The categories on the left narrow the list.

44
00:02:51,312 --> 00:02:57,515
The Filter box matches the start of a name, so typing asset leaves the asset_url card.

45
00:02:57,515 --> 00:03:00,482
Add puts that shortcode into the text.

46
00:03:00,944 --> 00:03:03,738
Its two tags have a space between them.

47
00:03:03,738 --> 00:03:08,828
We replace the space with the file name post-bg.jpg, so the shortcode points

48
00:03:08,828 --> 00:03:11,124
at a file in the media library.

49
00:03:11,590 --> 00:03:16,329
The asset_url shortcode gives only an address, with no picture.

50
00:03:16,329 --> 00:03:21,480
After publishing, the page shows the address of the file on the site.

51
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:30,154
Shortcodes work in the HTML body and the Markdown body of a content

52
00:03:30,154 --> 00:03:33,280
item, and in HTML fields and Markdown fields.

53
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:38,980
The Markdown editor with a toolbar has buttons named Insert Shortcode and Insert Image.

54
00:03:39,730 --> 00:03:44,782
You can also type a shortcode by hand, since the buttons only save typing.

55
00:03:44,782 --> 00:03:50,530
In the editor, a shortcode stays plain text, and the displayed page shows the result.

56
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:57,020
Shortcodes let your text carry a picture or an address that the site fills in.

57
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,410
Thanks for watching.

